-- title:
--   Descent of ideal membership along an injective substitution
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a noetherian commutative ring and $q\in\mathbb N$, and let $I$ be an ideal of $B[\![y_1,\dots,y_q]\!]=\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,q)\,B$ such that the quotient $B[\![y]\!]/I$ is finite and projective as a $B$-module. Let $d,n,m\in\mathbb N$ and let $a\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,n\to B[\![x_1,\dots,x_m]\!]$ be a family of power series all of whose constant coefficients vanish. Assume the substitution endomorphism on power series in the variables $\mathrm{Fin}\,n\sqcup\mathrm{Fin}\,d$, sending the $k$-th variable of the first block to $a_k$ read in the first block of $\mathrm{Fin}\,m\sqcup\mathrm{Fin}\,d$ and each variable of the second block to itself, has trivial kernel: any $H$ with zero image is zero. Let $V$ be a power series in the variables $(\mathrm{Fin}\,d\sqcup\mathrm{Fin}\,q)\sqcup\mathrm{Fin}\,n$, written $V(z,y,s)$, and suppose that its image under the substitution fixing all variables of the block $\mathrm{Fin}\,d\sqcup\mathrm{Fin}\,q$ and sending $s_k$ to $a_k$ in the variables $\mathrm{Fin}\,m$ lies in the ideal generated by the image of $I$ under the inclusion $y_l\mapsto X_{y_l}$. Then $V$ itself lies in the ideal of $B[\![z,y,s]\!]$ generated by the image of $I$ under the corresponding inclusion $y_l\mapsto X_{y_l}$.
--
--   This is the transfer step which allows invariance modulo the ideal $I$, checked after substituting the coordinates $a$, to be read back for a free set of parameters $s$; it uses that rings of multivariate formal power series in finitely many variables over a noetherian ring are noetherian ([`MvPowerSeries.isNoetherianRing_fin_of_isNoetherianRing`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.isNoetherianRing_fin_of_isNoetherianRing)). It is invoked in the construction of a commutative multivariate formal group law from invariant coordinates, [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_mvFormalGroup_isComm_isLawHom_of_invariant_coordinates`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_mvFormalGroup_isComm_isLawHom_of_invariant_coordinates).
-- source:
